From d30d402d985c296477ecd816973410dd3b2fad7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:12:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 07/19] xocl/p2p: use device_iommu_mapped() on Linux 6.13+

Mainline commit 6632863226d8 ("iommu: Remove iommu_present()", v6.13)
removed the bus-wide query used by p2p_read_addr_mgmtpf() to decide
whether the P2P BAR address may be handed to the management PF.

Guard: LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0) keeps
iommu_present(&pci_bus_type); checked against mainline v6.12 (has it)
and v6.13 (gone) <linux/iommu.h> and the 6.17.0-35 / 7.0.0-x headers.

Equivalence: iommu_present(&pci_bus_type) answered "is any IOMMU
instance registered" (drivers/iommu/iommu.c, v6.12); the per-device
query that remains, device_iommu_mapped(&pcidev->dev)
(available since 5.0, also on 6.8), answers "is this device's DMA
translated" (dev->iommu_group != NULL). On x86 with VT-d/AMD-Vi enabled
every PCI function is put in an IOMMU group, including in passthrough
mode (iommu=pt), and with the IOMMU disabled neither query is true, so
both give the same answer for the Alveo card. They can only differ when
an IOMMU is registered that does not cover this device; then 6.13+
reports the BAR, which is what the check is meant to decide. There is
no exported 6.13+ API that reproduces the bus-wide answer.

Upstream: same change as the p2p.c hunk of XRT commit f41db917c
("xocl: Fixes for compilation on kernel 6.16+").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
---
 driver/xocl/subdev/p2p.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/driver/xocl/subdev/p2p.c b/driver/xocl/subdev/p2p.c
index 171f7d8..b77f680 100644
--- a/driver/xocl/subdev/p2p.c
+++ b/driver/xocl/subdev/p2p.c
@@ -513,7 +513,12 @@ static void p2p_read_addr_mgmtpf(struct p2p *p2p)
 	mb_req->req = XCL_MAILBOX_REQ_READ_P2P_BAR_ADDR;
 	mb_p2p = (struct xcl_mailbox_p2p_bar_addr *)mb_req->data;
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 13, 0)
 	if (!iommu_present(&pci_bus_type)){
+#else
+	/* iommu_present() was removed in 6.13 (commit 6632863226d8) */
+	if (!device_iommu_mapped(&pcidev->dev)) {
+#endif
 		mb_p2p->p2p_bar_len = pci_resource_len(pcidev, p2p->p2p_bar_idx);
 		mb_p2p->p2p_bar_addr = pci_resource_start(pcidev,
 				p2p->p2p_bar_idx);
